            <ArticleTitle>Lipomatous hypertrophy of the interatrial septum: an unusual intraoperative finding.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Lipomatous hypertrophy of the interatrial septum was an incidental finding in a man of 45 undergoing coronary artery bypass grafting for unstable angina. He was not overweight and did not have any rhythm disturbances. The diagnosis was made on frozen section.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
